      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Albedo": {
        "mds:value": "a solar reflectance factor that relates the amount of diffuse radiation to global irradiation (0.15)",
        "mds:quote": "The albedo effect also indicates a low diffuse-to-global ratio, which is consistent with high cloud cover or pollution (Section III.B)."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Algorithm": {
        "mds:value": "The PVLib library includes several algorithms for calculating solar irradiance, and these can be combined in various ways to suit specific needs (Section III.J)."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Architecture": {
        "mds:value": "The Python-based PVlib was chosen due to its flexibility and open-source nature with a clean architecture using core and package objects (Section II)."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Capacity": {
        "mds:value": "The capacity is reduced after a damage event, with some PV systems experiencing a reduction in capacity by up to 4.3%."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Cell": {
        "mds:value": "A cell has a fill_factor greater than 0.95 indicating that up to more than one electron is captured for each photon absorbed by the material (Section III.G)."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/ClimateZone": {
        "mds:value": "the climate zone determines the type of insulation and cooling requirements in a PV system."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/ClosedCircuit": {
        "mds:value": "electricity is generated using the PV system in a closed circuit."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Comparison": {
        "mds:value": "a comparison of the PV performance under various conditions is made to evaluate the effectiveness of the different configurations."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Condition": {
        "mds:value": "PV system can operate in any environmental condition, including temperatures below 20°C at which they would normally not perform efficiently (Section I)."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Damage": {
        "mds:value": "damages in the PV system include crack in panel, hot spots and micro-cracks."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Data": {
        "mds:value": "Data on various input/output parameters can be stored in a database to evaluate performance (Section III.J).",
        "mds:quote": "input parameter values for the evaluation can then be changed and run using either Python or MATLAB."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Design": {
        "mds:value": "The efficiency of a PV system is influenced by its design, including factors such as location and number of panels (Section III.G)."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Diode": {
        "mds:value": "the ideal diode model describes the behavior of an ideal current source in series with an ideal diode."
      },
      "https://cwrusdle.bitbucket.io/mds/generic/Heterojunction": {
        "mds:value": "Heterojunction is a type of bipolar junction in a diode."
      },
